{
  "_comment": "OF26 follow-up, extended by FOUR-BIOME-BUILD. This is the SOURCE scripts/ui/tab_settings.gd draws its rows from: a hand-curated, always-complete list with exactly two testable spots per Meadows band, Cloudreach/Stormwood region, or Water island. All four shipped biomes are offered regardless of the realm the player is standing in or has discovered. Every row uses GameState.debug_teleport_to(x, z, realm_id, entry_id), the same real scene-change and grounding path tested by tests/smoke_realm_teleport.gd.",
  "_comment_bands": "Meadows band ids/boundaries are data/config/chapter_curve.json's own five `regions` (band1_lower_meadows .. band5_stronghold_approach), the file docs/specs/MEADOWS_PROGRESSION_SPEC.md section 3's prose bands actually compile down to in the shipped world (z_to boundaries, matched against scripts/world/world_perimeter.gd by tests/test_chapter_curve.gd). Every position below is a REAL authored place already used elsewhere in the game -- a map region/landmark centre from data/config/map_landmarks.json, or (band 5's approach) the first of the Hall's own approach_pylons in data/config/stronghold.json -- picked to be spread well apart within its band rather than clustered at one end of it, not invented for this list.",
  "_comment_cloudreach": "Cloudreach's own six authored regions (data/config/cloudreach_world.json's `regions`, ordered 1-6 per docs/biomes/cloudreach/BUILD_CLOUDREACH_CLIFFS_TO_COMPLETION.md section 11) each already carry exactly two landmarks inside their own `bounds` box -- verified by point-in-box against the live config, not guessed -- so both of that biome's spots per region are its own two named landmarks, position taken as (x, z) with the altitude (y) dropped: `debug_teleport_to` derives height from the destination world's own `ground_height_at`, exactly as every other row on this screen already does.",
  "_comment_stormwood": "Stormwood's six named regions come directly from stormwood_world.json. Two real landmarks per region are used so each row lands on authored ground and the locked late regions remain directly testable without manufacturing story flags.",
  "_comment_water": "Water's twelve islands come directly from water_world.json. Each has two authored safe destinations: landmark positions where two exist, otherwise one landmark plus a terrain-grounded arrival/departure safe position. Y is deliberately omitted because the destination world's ground_height_at supplies it.",
  "_comment_entry_ids": "`entry_id` is resolved at build time by GameState._debug_teleport_entry_id_for() from each realm's authored transition source: cloudreach_world.json, stormwood_world.json, water_world.json, or realm_transitions.json. It is not duplicated in this list, so re-authoring an arrival anchor updates the menu path from the same edit.",

